sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User Browser
    participant Dashboard as Dashboard UI
    participant Hooks as React Hooks
    participant Services as Frontend Services
    participant API as Backend API
    participant GitHub as GitHub Actions API
    participant Health as Health Endpoints
    participant WS as WebSocket Server
    participant DB as Database

    Note over User,DB: Initial Dashboard Load

    User->>Dashboard: Navigate to /dashboard/deployments
    Dashboard->>Hooks: Mount components
    Hooks->>Services: Fetch initial data

    par Parallel Data Fetching
        Services->>API: GET /api/deployments/status
        API->>GitHub: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs
        GitHub-->>API: Workflow runs data
        API->>DB: Query deployment history
        DB-->>API: Historical data
        API-->>Services: Current deployment status
        Services-->>Hooks: Update state
    and
        Services->>API: GET /api/health-checks/status
        API->>Health: GET /health, /ready, /live, /detailed
        Health-->>API: Health check results
        API-->>Services: Aggregated health status
        Services-->>Hooks: Update health state
    and
        Services->>API: GET /api/smoke-tests/results
        API->>GitHub: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs/{id}/jobs
        GitHub-->>API: Job details with test results
        API-->>Services: Smoke test results
        Services-->>Hooks: Update test state
    and
        Services->>API: GET /api/metrics/deployments
        API->>DB: Query metrics (last 30 days)
        DB-->>API: Aggregated metrics
        API-->>Services: Deployment analytics
        Services-->>Hooks: Update metrics state
    end

    Hooks-->>Dashboard: Render complete dashboard
    Dashboard-->>User: Display deployment status

    Note over User,DB: Real-time Updates via WebSocket

    Services->>WS: Connect to /ws/deployments
    WS-->>Services: Connection established
    Services->>WS: Subscribe to deployment:95c2fe1

    loop Real-time Monitoring (every 5-10s)
        GitHub->>WS: Workflow status update (webhook)
        WS->>DB: Store deployment event
        WS-->>Services: Broadcast deployment update
        Services-->>Hooks: Update state
        Hooks-->>Dashboard: Re-render affected components
        Dashboard-->>User: Live status update

        Health->>WS: Health check result (polling)
        WS-->>Services: Broadcast health update
        Services-->>Hooks: Update health state
        Hooks-->>Dashboard: Update health indicators
        Dashboard-->>User: Live health status
    end

    Note over User,DB: User Actions - Emergency Rollback

    User->>Dashboard: Click "Emergency Rollback"
    Dashboard->>Dashboard: Show confirmation dialog
    User->>Dashboard: Confirm rollback
    Dashboard->>Services: triggerRollback(environment, commitSha)
    Services->>API: POST /api/deployments/rollback
    API->>GitHub: POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows/{id}/dispatches
    GitHub-->>API: Workflow triggered
    API-->>Services: Rollback initiated
    Services-->>Hooks: Update state (status: rolling_back)
    Hooks-->>Dashboard: Show rollback progress

    loop Rollback Monitoring
        GitHub->>WS: Rollback workflow updates
        WS-->>Services: Broadcast rollback progress
        Services-->>Hooks: Update progress state
        Hooks-->>Dashboard: Update progress bar
        Dashboard-->>User: Live rollback status
    end

    GitHub->>WS: Rollback complete
    WS-->>Services: Broadcast completion
    Services-->>Hooks: Final state update
    Hooks-->>Dashboard: Show success message
    Dashboard-->>User: "Rollback completed in 1m 45s"

    Note over User,DB: Deployment History & Details

    User->>Dashboard: Click deployment "95c2fe1"
    Dashboard->>Services: fetchDeploymentDetails(95c2fe1)
    Services->>API: GET /api/deployments/95c2fe1

    par Fetch Detailed Information
        API->>GitHub: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs/{runId}
        GitHub-->>API: Complete run details
    and
        API->>GitHub: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs/{runId}/jobs
        GitHub-->>API: All jobs with steps
    and
        API->>DB: Query deployment metrics, logs, events
        DB-->>API: Complete deployment record
    end

    API-->>Services: Detailed deployment data
    Services-->>Hooks: Update detail state
    Hooks-->>Dashboard: Render detail view
    Dashboard-->>User: Show complete deployment details

    Note over User,DB: Error Troubleshooting

    User->>Dashboard: Click "View Error Logs"
    Dashboard->>Services: fetchErrorLogs(jobId)
    Services->>API: GET /api/github/jobs/{jobId}/logs
    API->>GitHub: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/jobs/{jobId}/logs
    GitHub-->>API: Complete job logs
    API->>API: Parse logs, extract errors
    API->>API: Categorize errors, suggest fixes
    API-->>Services: Formatted error data with remediation
    Services-->>Hooks: Update error state
    Hooks-->>Dashboard: Render error panel
    Dashboard-->>User: Show errors with suggested fixes

    Note over User,DB: Cleanup & Disconnect

    User->>Dashboard: Navigate away
    Dashboard->>Hooks: Unmount components
    Hooks->>Services: Cleanup subscriptions
    Services->>WS: Unsubscribe from deployment:95c2fe1
    Services->>WS: Disconnect
    WS-->>Services: Connection closed
